  "status_text": "A whole circuit of flips can be replaced by one shared list. Lean checked this for any rule connecting the input bits to all the required answers. If every gate is a NOT, each answer can read a fixed input, a free constant, or a flipped input from a single shared set. That set has size at most the smaller of the total gate budget and the NOT budget. Every choice that meets the rule gives a circuit, with one NOT per distinct flipped input. Next we ask what combining two inputs can buy (L-lib-1212).",
